{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785676669238,"sessionID":"ses_03d6082b8ffevm2f5lmWdFLskw","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"read_0","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-syu3u3ut/retort-02000dd611c2/TASK.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-syu3u3ut/retort-02000dd611c2/TASK.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Brazilian Soccer MCP Server - Specification\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: \n5: This document specifies the requirements for creating an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that provides a knowledge graph interface for Brazilian soccer data. The server should enable natural language queries about players, teams, matches, and competitions using the provided datasets.\n6: \n7: ---\n8: \n9: ## Purpose\n10: \n11: - **Use Case**: Demo/Non-commercial use\n12: - **Goal**: Create an MCP server that can answer natural language questions about Brazilian soccer\n13: - **Integration**: MCP server connected to an LLM for query processing\n14: \n15: ---\n16: \n17: ## Provided Data\n18: \n19: The following datasets are included in `data/kaggle/` and must be used:\n20: \n21: ### Match Data\n22: \n23: #### 1. Brasileirão Serie A Matches\n24: **File**: `Brasileirao_Matches.csv` (4,180 matches)\n25: **Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/ricardomattos05/jogos-do-campeonato-brasileiro\n26: **License**: CC BY 4.0\n27: \n28: | Column | Description |\n29: |--------|-------------|\n30: | datetime | Match date and time |\n31: | home_team | Home team name with state suffix (e.g., \"Palmeiras-SP\") |\n32: | home_team_state | State abbreviation |\n33: | away_team | Away team name with state suffix |\n34: | away_team_state | State abbreviation |\n35: | home_goal | Goals scored by home team |\n36: | away_goal | Goals scored by away team |\n37: | season | Year of the season |\n38: | round | Match round number |\n39: \n40: #### 2. Copa do Brasil Matches\n41: **File**: `Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv` (1,337 matches)\n42: **Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/ricardomattos05/jogos-do-campeonato-brasileiro\n43: **License**: CC BY 4.0\n44: \n45: | Column | Description |\n46: |--------|-------------|\n47: | round | Cup round |\n48: | datetime | Match date and time |\n49: | home_team | Home team name |\n50: | away_team | Away team name |\n51: | home_goal | Home team goals |\n52: | away_goal | Away team goals |\n53: | season | Year |\n54: \n55: #### 3. Copa Libertadores Matches\n56: **File**: `Libertadores_Matches.csv` (1,255 matches)\n57: **Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/ricardomattos05/jogos-do-campeonato-brasileiro\n58: **License**: CC BY 4.0\n59: \n60: | Column | Description |\n61: |--------|-------------|\n62: | datetime | Match date and time |\n63: | home_team | Home team name |\n64: | away_team | Away team name |\n65: | home_goal | Home team goals |\n66: | away_goal | Away team goals |\n67: | season | Year |\n68: | stage | Tournament stage (group stage, knockout, etc.) |\n69: \n70: #### 4. Extended Match Statistics\n71: **File**: `BR-Football-Dataset.csv` (10,296 matches)\n72: **Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/cuecacuela/brazilian-football-matches\n73: **License**: CC0 Public Domain\n74: \n75: | Column | Description |\n76: |--------|-------------|\n77: | tournament | Competition name |\n78: | home | Home team |\n79: | away | Away team |\n80: | home_goal, away_goal | Final scores |\n81: | home_corner, away_corner | Corner kicks |\n82: | home_attack, away_attack | Attacks |\n83: | home_shots, away_shots | Shots |\n84: | time | Kick-off time |\n85: | date | Match date |\n86: | ht_result, at_result | Half-time results |\n87: | total_corners | Total corners in match |\n88: \n89: #### 5. Historical Brasileirão (2003-2019)\n90: **File**: `novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv` (6,886 matches)\n91: **Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/macedojleo/campeonato-brasileiro-2003-a-2019\n92: **License**: CC BY 4.0\n93: \n94: | Column | Description |\n95: |--------|-------------|\n96: | ID | Unique match identifier |\n97: | Data | Match date (DD/MM/YYYY format) |\n98: | Ano | Year |\n99: | Rodada | Round number |\n100: | Equipe_mandante | Home team |\n101: | Equipe_visitante | Away team |\n102: | Gols_mandante | Home goals |\n103: | Gols_visitante | Away goals |\n104: | Mandante_UF, Visitante_UF | Team states |\n105: | Vencedor | Winner (Mandante/Visitante/Empate) |\n106: | Arena | Stadium name |\n107: \n108: ### Player Data\n109: \n110: #### 6. FIFA Player Database\n111: **File**: `fifa_data.csv` (18,207 players)\n112: **Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/youssefelbadry10/fifa-players-data\n113: **License**: Apache 2.0\n114: \n115: Key columns include:\n116: | Column | Description |\n117: |--------|-------------|\n118: | ID | Unique player identifier |\n119: | Name | Player name |\n120: | Age | Player age |\n121: | Nationality | Country |\n122: | Overall | FIFA overall rating |\n123: | Potential | FIFA potential rating |\n124: | Club | Current club |\n125: | Position | Playing position |\n126: | Jersey Number | Shirt number |\n127: | Height, Weight | Physical attributes |\n128: | Various skill ratings | Crossing, Finishing, Dribbling, etc. |\n129: \n130: ---\n131: \n132: ## Additional Data Sources (Optional)\n133: \n134: These sources may be used to supplement the provided data:\n135: \n136: ### API-Football\n137: - **URL**: https://dashboard.api-football.com/\n138: - **Features**: Current season data, live scores\n139: - **Free tier**: Limited daily requests\n140: \n141: ### TheSportsDB\n142: - **URL**: https://www.thesportsdb.com/documentation\n143: - **Features**: Team logos, player photos, artwork\n144: - **Free tier**: Test key \"123\", 2 requests/minute limit\n145: \n146: ### Wikipedia/DBpedia\n147: - Historical context and notable player/team information\n148: \n149: ---\n150: \n151: ## Required Capabilities\n152: \n153: The MCP server must support queries in these categories:\n154: \n155: ### 1. Match Queries\n156: \n157: **Find matches by criteria:**\n158: - By team (home, away, or either)\n159: - By date range\n160: - By competition (Brasileirão, Copa do Brasil, Libertadores)\n161: - By season\n162: \n163: **Example questions:**\n164: - \"Show me all Flamengo vs Fluminense matches\"\n165: - \"What matches did Palmeiras play in 2023?\"\n166: - \"Find all Copa do Brasil finals\"\n167: \n168: **Example answer format:**\n169: ```\n170: Flamengo vs Fluminense (Fla-Flu derby):\n171: - 2023-09-03: Flamengo 2-1 Fluminense (Brasileirão Round 22)\n172: - 2023-05-28: Fluminense 1-0 Flamengo (Brasileirão Round 8)\n173: - ... (15 more matches in dataset)\n174: \n175: Head-to-head in dataset: Flamengo 12 wins, Fluminense 8 wins, 7 draws\n176: ```\n177: \n178: ### 2. Team Queries\n179: \n180: **Find team information:**\n181: - Match history and statistics\n182: - Win/loss/draw records\n183: - Goals scored/conceded\n184: - Performance by competition\n185: \n186: **Example questions:**\n187: - \"What is Corinthians' home record in 2022?\"\n188: - \"Which team scored the most goals in Serie A 2023?\"\n189: - \"Compare Palmeiras and Santos head-to-head\"\n190: \n191: **Example answer format:**\n192: ```\n193: Corinthians home record (2022 Brasileirão):\n194: - Matches: 19\n195: - Wins: 11, Draws: 5, Losses: 3\n196: - Goals For: 28, Goals Against: 15\n197: - Win rate: 57.9%\n198: ```\n199: \n200: ### 3. Player Queries\n201: \n202: **Find player information:**\n203: - Search by name\n204: - Filter by nationality (especially Brazilian players)\n205: - Filter by club (especially Brazilian clubs)\n206: - Player ratings and attributes\n207: \n208: **Example questions:**\n209: - \"Find all Brazilian players in the dataset\"\n210: - \"Who are the highest-rated players at Flamengo?\"\n211: - \"Show me all forwards from São Paulo FC\"\n212: \n213: **Example answer format:**\n214: ```\n215: Top-rated Brazilian players in dataset:\n216: 1. Neymar Jr - Overall: 92, Position: LW, Club: Paris Saint-Germain\n217: 2. Alisson - Overall: 89, Position: GK, Club: Liverpool\n218: 3. Casemiro - Overall: 89, Position: CDM, Club: Real Madrid\n219: ...\n220: \n221: Brazilian players at Brazilian clubs:\n222: - Flamengo: 8 players (avg rating: 74)\n223: - Palmeiras: 7 players (avg rating: 72)\n224: ...\n225: ```\n226: \n227: ### 4. Competition Queries\n228: \n229: **Find competition information:**\n230: - Standings by season (calculated from match results)\n231: - Top scorers (if inferable from data)\n232: - Match schedules and results\n233: \n234: **Example questions:**\n235: - \"Who won the 2019 Brasileirão?\"\n236: - \"Show the 2018 Copa Libertadores bracket\"\n237: - \"Which teams were relegated in 2020?\"\n238: \n239: **Example answer format:**\n240: ```\n241: 2019 Brasileirão Final Standings (calculated from matches):\n242: 1. Flamengo - 90 pts (28W, 6D, 4L) - Champion\n243: 2. Santos - 74 pts (22W, 8D, 8L)\n244: 3. Palmeiras - 74 pts (21W, 11D, 6L)\n245: ...\n246: ```\n247: \n248: ### 5. Statistical Analysis\n249: \n250: **Calculate aggregated statistics:**\n251: - Goals per match averages\n252: - Team performance trends\n253: - Head-to-head records\n254: - Home vs away performance\n255: \n256: **Example questions:**\n257: - \"What's the average goals per match in the Brasileirão?\"\n258: - \"Which team has the best away record?\"\n259: - \"Show me the biggest wins in the dataset\"\n260: \n261: **Example answer format:**\n262: ```\n263: Biggest victories in Brasileirão (provided data):\n264: 1. 2012-05-27: Santos 8-0 Bolivar (Libertadores)\n265: 2. 2015-09-13: Palmeiras 6-0 São Paulo\n266: 3. 2019-10-27: Flamengo 5-0 Grêmio\n267: ...\n268: \n269: Average goals per match: 2.47\n270: Home win rate: 47.3%\n271: ```\n272: \n273: ---\n274: \n275: ## Sample Questions and Expected Behaviors\n276: \n277: ### Simple Lookups\n278: | Question | Expected Behavior |\n279: |----------|-------------------|\n280: | \"When did Flamengo last play Corinthians?\" | Search match data for most recent match between these teams |\n281: | \"What was the score?\" | Return home_goal and away_goal |\n282: | \"Who is Gabriel Barbosa?\" | Search FIFA player data by name |\n283: \n284: ### Relationship Queries\n285: | Question | Expected Behavior |\n286: |----------|-------------------|\n287: | \"Which players play for Flamengo?\" | Filter FIFA data by Club containing \"Flamengo\" |\n288: | \"Show me all derbies in 2023\" | Find matches where teams are traditional rivals |\n289: | \"What competitions has Palmeiras played in?\" | Search all match files for Palmeiras matches |\n290: \n291: ### Analytical Queries\n292: | Question | Expected Behavior |\n293: |----------|-------------------|\n294: | \"Which team has the best home record?\" | Calculate win rates from match data |\n295: | \"Who are the top Brazilian players?\" | Filter and sort FIFA data |\n296: | \"Compare the 2018 and 2019 seasons\" | Aggregate statistics across seasons |\n297: \n298: ---\n299: \n300: ## Data Quality Notes\n301: \n302: ### Team Name Variations\n303: The datasets use different naming conventions:\n304: - With state suffix: \"Palmeiras-SP\", \"Flamengo-RJ\"\n305: - Without suffix: \"Palmeiras\", \"Flamengo\"\n306: - Full names: \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\"\n307: \n308: **Implementation should normalize team names for consistent matching.**\n309: \n310: ### Date Formats\n311: - ISO format: \"2023-09-24\"\n312: - Brazilian format: \"29/03/2003\"\n313: - With time: \"2012-05-19 18:30:00\"\n314: \n315: **Implementation should handle multiple date formats.**\n316: \n317: ### Character Encoding\n318: Brazilian Portuguese text includes special characters:\n319: - Accents: São Paulo, Grêmio, Avaí\n320: - Cedilla: Fortaleza Esporte Clube\n321: \n322: **Implementation should handle UTF-8 encoding.**\n323: \n324: ---\n325: \n326: ## Success Criteria\n327: \n328: ### Functional Requirements\n329: - [ ] Can search and return match data from all provided CSV files\n330: - [ ] Can search and return player data\n331: - [ ] Can calculate basic statistics (wins, losses, goals)\n332: - [ ] Can compare teams head-to-head\n333: - [ ] Handles team name variations correctly\n334: - [ ] Returns properly formatted responses\n335: \n336: ### Query Performance\n337: - [ ] Simple lookups respond in < 2 seconds\n338: - [ ] Aggregate queries respond in < 5 seconds\n339: - [ ] No timeout errors\n340: \n341: ### Data Coverage\n342: - [ ] All 6 CSV files are loadable and queryable\n343: - [ ] At least 20 sample questions can be answered\n344: - [ ] Cross-file queries work (e.g., player + match data)\n345: \n346: ---\n347: \n348: ## Testing Approach\n349: \n350: Use BDD (Behavior-Driven Development) test scenarios:\n351: \n352: ```gherkin\n353: Feature: Match Queries\n354: \n355: Scenario: Find matches between two teams\n356:   Given the match data is loaded\n357:   When I search for matches between \"Flamengo\" and \"Fluminense\"\n358:   Then I should receive a list of matches\n359:   And each match should have date, scores, and competition\n360: \n361: Scenario: Get team statistics\n362:   Given the match data is loaded\n363:   When I request statistics for \"Palmeiras\" in season \"2023\"\n364:   Then I should receive wins, losses, draws, and goals\n365: ```\n366: \n367: ---\n368: \n369: ## Document Information\n370: - **Version**: 2.0\n371: - **Purpose**: Specification for Brazilian Soccer MCP Server benchmark\n372: - **Data**: Pre-downloaded Kaggle datasets included in repository\n373: - **Status**: Ready for implementation\n374: \n375: ---\n376: \n377: ## References\n378: \n379: ### MCP Protocol\n380: - Documentation: https://modelcontextprotocol.io\n381: \n382: ### Data Sources\n383: - Kaggle Brazilian Soccer: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/ricardomattos05/jogos-do-campeonato-brasileiro\n384: - Brazilian Football Matches: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/cuecacuela/brazilian-football-matches\n385: - Campeonato Brasileiro 2003-2019: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/macedojleo/campeonato-brasileiro-2003-a-2019\n386: - FIFA Players: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/youssefelbadry10/fifa-players-data\n387: \n388: ### Optional APIs\n389: - API-Football: https://dashboard.api-football.com/\n390: - TheSportsDB: https://www.thesportsdb.com/documentation\n\n(End of file - total 390 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Brazilian Soccer MCP Server - Specification\n\n## Overview\n\nThis document specifies the requirements for creating an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that provides a knowledge graph interface for Brazilian soccer data. The server should enable natural language queries about players, teams, matches, and competitions using the provided datasets.\n\n---\n\n## Purpose\n\n- **Use Case**: Demo/Non-commercial use\n- **Goal**: Create an MCP server that can answer natural language questions about Brazilian soccer\n- **Integration**: MCP server connected to an LLM for query processing\n\n---\n\n## Provided Data\n\nThe following datasets are included in `data/kaggle/` and must be used:\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-syu3u3ut/retort-02000dd611c2/TASK.md","text":"# Brazilian Soccer MCP Server - Specification\n\n## Overview\n\nThis document specifies the requirements for creating an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that provides a knowledge graph interface for Brazilian soccer data. The server should enable natural language queries about players, teams, matches, and competitions using the provided datasets.\n\n---\n\n## Purpose\n\n- **Use Case**: Demo/Non-commercial use\n- **Goal**: Create an MCP server that can answer natural language questions about Brazilian soccer\n- **Integration**: MCP server connected to an LLM for query processing\n\n---\n\n## Provided Data\n\nThe following datasets are included in `data/kaggle/` and must be used:\n\n### Match Data\n\n#### 1. Brasileirão Serie A Matches\n**File**: `Brasileirao_Matches.csv` (4,180 matches)\n**Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/ricardomattos05/jogos-do-campeonato-brasileiro\n**License**: CC BY 4.0\n\n| Column | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| datetime | Match date and time |\n| home_team | Home team name with state suffix (e.g., \"Palmeiras-SP\") |\n| home_team_state | State abbreviation |\n| away_team | Away team name with state suffix |\n| away_team_state | State abbreviation |\n| home_goal | Goals scored by home team |\n| away_goal | Goals scored by away team |\n| season | Year of the season |\n| round | Match round number |\n\n#### 2. Copa do Brasil Matches\n**File**: `Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv` (1,337 matches)\n**Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/ricardomattos05/jogos-do-campeonato-brasileiro\n**License**: CC BY 4.0\n\n| Column | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| round | Cup round |\n| datetime | Match date and time |\n| home_team | Home team name |\n| away_team | Away team name |\n| home_goal | Home team goals |\n| away_goal | Away team goals |\n| season | Year |\n\n#### 3. Copa Libertadores Matches\n**File**: `Libertadores_Matches.csv` (1,255 matches)\n**Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/ricardomattos05/jogos-do-campeonato-brasileiro\n**License**: CC BY 4.0\n\n| Column | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| datetime | Match date and time |\n| home_team | Home team name |\n| away_team | Away team name |\n| home_goal | Home team goals |\n| away_goal | Away team goals |\n| season | Year |\n| stage | Tournament stage (group stage, knockout, etc.) |\n\n#### 4. Extended Match Statistics\n**File**: `BR-Football-Dataset.csv` (10,296 matches)\n**Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/cuecacuela/brazilian-football-matches\n**License**: CC0 Public Domain\n\n| Column | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| tournament | Competition name |\n| home | Home team |\n| away | Away team |\n| home_goal, away_goal | Final scores |\n| home_corner, away_corner | Corner kicks |\n| home_attack, away_attack | Attacks |\n| home_shots, away_shots | Shots |\n| time | Kick-off time |\n| date | Match date |\n| ht_result, at_result | Half-time results |\n| total_corners | Total corners in match |\n\n#### 5. Historical Brasileirão (2003-2019)\n**File**: `novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv` (6,886 matches)\n**Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/macedojleo/campeonato-brasileiro-2003-a-2019\n**License**: CC BY 4.0\n\n| Column | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| ID | Unique match identifier |\n| Data | Match date (DD/MM/YYYY format) |\n| Ano | Year |\n| Rodada | Round number |\n| Equipe_mandante | Home team |\n| Equipe_visitante | Away team |\n| Gols_mandante | Home goals |\n| Gols_visitante | Away goals |\n| Mandante_UF, Visitante_UF | Team states |\n| Vencedor | Winner (Mandante/Visitante/Empate) |\n| Arena | Stadium name |\n\n### Player Data\n\n#### 6. FIFA Player Database\n**File**: `fifa_data.csv` (18,207 players)\n**Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/youssefelbadry10/fifa-players-data\n**License**: Apache 2.0\n\nKey columns include:\n| Column | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| ID | Unique player identifier |\n| Name | Player name |\n| Age | Player age |\n| Nationality | Country |\n| Overall | FIFA overall rating |\n| Potential | FIFA potential rating |\n| Club | Current club |\n| Position | Playing position |\n| Jersey Number | Shirt number |\n| Height, Weight | Physical attributes |\n| Various skill ratings | Crossing, Finishing, Dribbling, etc. |\n\n---\n\n## Additional Data Sources (Optional)\n\nThese sources may be used to supplement the provided data:\n\n### API-Football\n- **URL**: https://dashboard.api-football.com/\n- **Features**: Current season data, live scores\n- **Free tier**: Limited daily requests\n\n### TheSportsDB\n- **URL**: https://www.thesportsdb.com/documentation\n- **Features**: Team logos, player photos, artwork\n- **Free tier**: Test key \"123\", 2 requests/minute limit\n\n### Wikipedia/DBpedia\n- Historical context and notable player/team information\n\n---\n\n## Required Capabilities\n\nThe MCP server must support queries in these categories:\n\n### 1. Match Queries\n\n**Find matches by criteria:**\n- By team (home, away, or either)\n- By date range\n- By competition (Brasileirão, Copa do Brasil, Libertadores)\n- By season\n\n**Example questions:**\n- \"Show me all Flamengo vs Fluminense matches\"\n- \"What matches did Palmeiras play in 2023?\"\n- \"Find all Copa do Brasil finals\"\n\n**Example answer format:**\n```\nFlamengo vs Fluminense (Fla-Flu derby):\n- 2023-09-03: Flamengo 2-1 Fluminense (Brasileirão Round 22)\n- 2023-05-28: Fluminense 1-0 Flamengo (Brasileirão Round 8)\n- ... (15 more matches in dataset)\n\nHead-to-head in dataset: Flamengo 12 wins, Fluminense 8 wins, 7 draws\n```\n\n### 2. Team Queries\n\n**Find team information:**\n- Match history and statistics\n- Win/loss/draw records\n- Goals scored/conceded\n- Performance by competition\n\n**Example questions:**\n- \"What is Corinthians' home record in 2022?\"\n- \"Which team scored the most goals in Serie A 2023?\"\n- \"Compare Palmeiras and Santos head-to-head\"\n\n**Example answer format:**\n```\nCorinthians home record (2022 Brasileirão):\n- Matches: 19\n- Wins: 11, Draws: 5, Losses: 3\n- Goals For: 28, Goals Against: 15\n- Win rate: 57.9%\n```\n\n### 3. Player Queries\n\n**Find player information:**\n- Search by name\n- Filter by nationality (especially Brazilian players)\n- Filter by club (especially Brazilian clubs)\n- Player ratings and attributes\n\n**Example questions:**\n- \"Find all Brazilian players in the dataset\"\n- \"Who are the highest-rated players at Flamengo?\"\n- \"Show me all forwards from São Paulo FC\"\n\n**Example answer format:**\n```\nTop-rated Brazilian players in dataset:\n1. Neymar Jr - Overall: 92, Position: LW, Club: Paris Saint-Germain\n2. Alisson - Overall: 89, Position: GK, Club: Liverpool\n3. Casemiro - Overall: 89, Position: CDM, Club: Real Madrid\n...\n\nBrazilian players at Brazilian clubs:\n- Flamengo: 8 players (avg rating: 74)\n- Palmeiras: 7 players (avg rating: 72)\n...\n```\n\n### 4. Competition Queries\n\n**Find competition information:**\n- Standings by season (calculated from match results)\n- Top scorers (if inferable from data)\n- Match schedules and results\n\n**Example questions:**\n- \"Who won the 2019 Brasileirão?\"\n- \"Show the 2018 Copa Libertadores bracket\"\n- \"Which teams were relegated in 2020?\"\n\n**Example answer format:**\n```\n2019 Brasileirão Final Standings (calculated from matches):\n1. Flamengo - 90 pts (28W, 6D, 4L) - Champion\n2. Santos - 74 pts (22W, 8D, 8L)\n3. Palmeiras - 74 pts (21W, 11D, 6L)\n...\n```\n\n### 5. Statistical Analysis\n\n**Calculate aggregated statistics:**\n- Goals per match averages\n- Team performance trends\n- Head-to-head records\n- Home vs away performance\n\n**Example questions:**\n- \"What's the average goals per match in the Brasileirão?\"\n- \"Which team has the best away record?\"\n- \"Show me the biggest wins in the dataset\"\n\n**Example answer format:**\n```\nBiggest victories in Brasileirão (provided data):\n1. 2012-05-27: Santos 8-0 Bolivar (Libertadores)\n2. 2015-09-13: Palmeiras 6-0 São Paulo\n3. 2019-10-27: Flamengo 5-0 Grêmio\n...\n\nAverage goals per match: 2.47\nHome win rate: 47.3%\n```\n\n---\n\n## Sample Questions and Expected Behaviors\n\n### Simple Lookups\n| Question | Expected Behavior |\n|----------|-------------------|\n| \"When did Flamengo last play Corinthians?\" | Search match data for most recent match between these teams |\n| \"What was the score?\" | Return home_goal and away_goal |\n| \"Who is Gabriel Barbosa?\" | Search FIFA player data by name |\n\n### Relationship Queries\n| Question | Expected Behavior |\n|----------|-------------------|\n| \"Which players play for Flamengo?\" | Filter FIFA data by Club containing \"Flamengo\" |\n| \"Show me all derbies in 2023\" | Find matches where teams are traditional rivals |\n| \"What competitions has Palmeiras played in?\" | Search all match files for Palmeiras matches |\n\n### Analytical Queries\n| Question | Expected Behavior |\n|----------|-------------------|\n| \"Which team has the best home record?\" | Calculate win rates from match data |\n| \"Who are the top Brazilian players?\" | Filter and sort FIFA data |\n| \"Compare the 2018 and 2019 seasons\" | Aggregate statistics across seasons |\n\n---\n\n## Data Quality Notes\n\n### Team Name Variations\nThe datasets use different naming conventions:\n- With state suffix: \"Palmeiras-SP\", \"Flamengo-RJ\"\n- Without suffix: \"Palmeiras\", \"Flamengo\"\n- Full names: \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\"\n\n**Implementation should normalize team names for consistent matching.**\n\n### Date Formats\n- ISO format: \"2023-09-24\"\n- Brazilian format: \"29/03/2003\"\n- With time: \"2012-05-19 18:30:00\"\n\n**Implementation should handle multiple date formats.**\n\n### Character Encoding\nBrazilian Portuguese text includes special characters:\n- Accents: São Paulo, Grêmio, Avaí\n- Cedilla: Fortaleza Esporte Clube\n\n**Implementation should handle UTF-8 encoding.**\n\n---\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n### Functional Requirements\n- [ ] Can search and return match data from all provided CSV files\n- [ ] Can search and return player data\n- [ ] Can calculate basic statistics (wins, losses, goals)\n- [ ] Can compare teams head-to-head\n- [ ] Handles team name variations correctly\n- [ ] Returns properly formatted responses\n\n### Query Performance\n- [ ] Simple lookups respond in < 2 seconds\n- [ ] Aggregate queries respond in < 5 seconds\n- [ ] No timeout errors\n\n### Data Coverage\n- [ ] All 6 CSV files are loadable and queryable\n- [ ] At least 20 sample questions can be answered\n- [ ] Cross-file queries work (e.g., player + match data)\n\n---\n\n## Testing Approach\n\nUse BDD (Behavior-Driven Development) test scenarios:\n\n```gherkin\nFeature: Match Queries\n\nScenario: Find matches between two teams\n  Given the match data is loaded\n  When I search for matches between \"Flamengo\" and \"Fluminense\"\n  Then I should receive a list of matches\n  And each match should have date, scores, and competition\n\nScenario: Get team statistics\n  Given the match data is loaded\n  When I request statistics for \"Palmeiras\" in season \"2023\"\n  Then I should receive wins, losses, draws, and goals\n```\n\n---\n\n## Document Information\n- **Version**: 2.0\n- **Purpose**: Specification for Brazilian Soccer MCP Server benchmark\n- **Data**: Pre-downloaded Kaggle datasets included in repository\n- **Status**: Ready for implementation\n\n---\n\n## References\n\n### MCP Protocol\n- Documentation: https://modelcontextprotocol.io\n\n### Data Sources\n- Kaggle Brazilian Soccer: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/ricardomattos05/jogos-do-campeonato-brasileiro\n- Brazilian Football Matches: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/cuecacuela/brazilian-football-matches\n- Campeonato Brasileiro 2003-2019: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/macedojleo/campeonato-brasileiro-2003-a-2019\n- FIFA Players: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/youssefelbadry10/fifa-players-data\n\n### Optional APIs\n- API-Football: https://dashboard.api-football.com/\n- TheSportsDB: https://www.thesportsdb.com/documentation","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":390,"totalLines":390,"truncated":false}},"title":"TASK.md","time":{"start":1785676669228,"end":1785676669235}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me start by reading TASK.md to understand what's being asked.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_fc29f9db7001c2IYCRL0OmhCT3","sessionID":"ses_03d6082b8ffevm2f5lmWdFLskw","messageID":"msg_fc29f7e20001veQZI1dppnx6GL"}}
