{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785676719111,"sessionID":"ses_03d6082b8ffevm2f5lmWdFLskw","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"bash_9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" --max-time 15 https://api.nuget.org/v3/index.json"},"output":"200","metadata":{"output":"200","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" --max-time 15 https://api.nuget.org/v3/index.json","time":{"start":1785676719107,"end":1785676719111}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The environment has .NET 10 SDK. Good.\n\nNow let me plan the project:\n\n1. **Solution structure**:\n   - `BrazilianSoccerMcp.sln`\n   - `src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/` — MCP server (console app, stdio transport)\n   - `tests/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Tests/` — xUnit tests with BDD-style scenarios\n\n2. **MCP server**: Use the official C# MCP SDK — `ModelContextProtocol` NuGet package. Let me check what's available. The official package is `ModelContextProtocol` (preview). For stdio server: `ModelContextProtocol` package with `Host.CreateApplicationBuilder`, `builder.Services.AddMcpServer().WithStdioServerTransport().WithToolsFromAssembly()`.\n\n   Requires NuGet.org access. Let me check if network is available for NuGet restore.\n\n3. **Data layer**:\n   - Load CSVs with a simple CSV parser (handle quoted fields). Could use CsvHelper package, but to keep dependencies minimal, write a simple parser. Actually CsvHelper is convenient, but network may be limited. Let me first check NuGet connectivity.\n\n4. **Tools to expose** (MCP tools):\n   - `find_matches` — by team(s), date range, competition, season\n   - `head_to_head` — two teams\n   - `team_statistics` — team record by season/competition/home-away\n   - `team_matches` — match history for a team\n   - `search_players` — by name, nationality, club, position\n   - `top_players` — filter/sort by rating\n   - `competition_standings` — calculated standings by season\n   - `competition_seasons` — list available seasons/competitions\n   - `match_statistics` — aggregate stats (avg goals, home win rate, biggest wins)\n   - `compare_teams` — head-to-head comparison\n\n5. **Team name normalization**: strip state suffixes like \"-SP\", \" - MG\", accents-insensitive matching, lowercase.\n\nLet me check NuGet connectivity first, and check what version of the ModelContextProtocol package is available.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_fc2a05e57001gy5CH7HSnz2fNH","sessionID":"ses_03d6082b8ffevm2f5lmWdFLskw","messageID":"msg_fc2a01b6f00138lj0LYEeyNQr3"}}
